{
 "format": "dpmg-mission/1",
 "name": "Loopback: port walk, six cable moves",
 "notes": "One G40 and one cable with the pad, moved six times. Before each move nothing is keyed for 90 s (60 s gap, then a 30 s Decode step): the radio changes jacks and the cable is moved then. After it one FSK message naming the jacks is keyed for 13 s at TX attenuation 30 dB. Cable for each move, TX jack to RX jack: 1: TRx1B to TRx1A; 2: TRx2B to TRx1A; 3: TRx1A to TRx1B; 4: TRx2A to TRx1B; 5: TRx1B to TRx2A; 6: TRx1A to TRx2B. The cable for move 1 can be fitted before Run mission.",
 "authorization": {
  "reference": "BENCH-LOOPBACK",
  "note": "cabled bench loopback: TX jack to RX jack through a pad, no antenna, no amplifier"
 },
 "anchor": {
  "mode": "on_tx"
 },
